# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Install to /etc/radar/payout.env (root-owned, 0640, group radar-payout).
#
# The payout process pays each claimed, unpaid contest week from the creator
# vault to the claimed address, and nothing else. Two things it needs are set
# in the unit rather than here -- the key's PATH (never the key) and the
# contest directory -- so that this file carries no secret and the key file's
# mode is the only thing standing between it and the rest of the box.
#
# Deny by default: with this unset the process pays nothing and says so. A
# default endpoint would be a spending path nobody chose.
#
# Direct RPC, never the x402 lane (AGENTS.md rule 7). The same endpoint the
# recorder uses is fine; the payout makes four calls a week.
#
# RADAR_RPC_URL=

# The smallest prize worth paying, in lamports. Rolls over below it.
#
# Design 0007 J2 and design 0009 L4 both say a floor with rollover. 100000000
# is 0.1 SOL, the figure both name; the number is the operator's, and this file
# ships it commented so it is a choice rather than a default.
#
# **Unset means no floor**, which pays out whatever a week collected. That is
# not rule 8 being bent: a floor is not a permission, it is a threshold below
# which money is withheld from the person who won it, and the safe direction is
# paying them. The process prints which it is using on every run, so a typo is
# visible rather than silent.
#
# A week below the floor stays unpaid and its prize rolls into the next week.
# The history page says so, and the winner is not asked to claim twice.
#
# RADAR_PAYOUT_FLOOR_LAMPORTS=100000000
